WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:01.410
BRIAN GRANT: Hi,
I'm Brian Grant.

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.120
I'm a Principal
Engineer at Google.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.280
I'm also a founding member of
the CNCF Technical Oversight

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.150
Committee.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.110
I just came off of a Q&amp;A
panel for the CNCF TOC.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:20.760
The TOC's job is to curate the
set of projects in the CNCF

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.790
to make sure that
they help advance

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.580
the cloud-native mission
of the foundation,

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.730
and also to help those
projects succeed.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.250
So that latter part,
helping the project succeed,

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.740
is an increasing
focus of the TOC

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.440
as we try to figure
out how to identify

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.930
what services the projects
need from the foundation

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.860
and how we can help the projects
attract new contributors

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.012
and maintainers.

00:00:45.012 --> 00:00:46.470
If you look at the
set of projects,

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:52.350
like Kuberetes, Prometheus,
Fluentd, GRPC, OpenTracing

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:55.860
and OpenTelemtry is a
recent project that Google's

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.980
been involved with, that
portfolio of projects

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.570
is really about helping
operators, users,

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:06.180
developers manage applications
with high velocity at scale

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:09.940
predictably and safely with
minimal amounts of toil.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.880
So as we look towards the
future with additional projects

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.910
that we might take
into the foundation,

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:18.720
we'll be looking for projects
to fill gaps in that portfolio

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.110
where users,
operators, developers

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:26.400
really need a solution that
fits with the other projects

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.310
we have.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:31.160
So if you're interested in
talking about those topics

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:34.030
and you're here at Keep Time,
come by the Google Cloud booth.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:34.590
Thank you.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.640
[MUSIC PLAYING]

